// Array returns travel through a caller-allocated slot, the same convention the
// struct-return fix introduced. Before that convention covered arrays, the
// callee alloca'd the array and returned a pointer into its own frame; the
// frame died and the caller read garbage. Elements are asymmetric and every one
// is asserted, because element 0 survived the dangling read and a first-element
// check would have passed while elements 1+ were garbage.
fnc: [3: t64] make() { [11, 22, 33] }
r: [3: t64] = make()
print(r:[0])
print(r:[1])
print(r:[2])
